{"term":"assert","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:67747aacc2e96f675b","definition":"To declare with assurance or plainly and strongly; to state positively.","example":"Numerous experimental tests and other observations have been offered in favor of animal mind reading, and although many scientists are skeptical, others assert that humans are not the only species capable of representing what others do and don’t perceive and know.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["affirm","asseverate","aver","avow"],"antonyms":["remit","deny","deassert"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["assertability","assertable","asserter","assertive","assertment","assert oneself","assertor","counterassert","misassert","overassert","reassert","unassert"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assert#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a52d6c1cdd5f518b80","definition":"To use or exercise and thereby prove the existence of.","example":"to assert one's authority","pos":"verb","synonyms":["exert"],"antonyms":["remit","deny","deassert"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["assertability","assertable","asserter","assertive","assertment","assert oneself","assertor","counterassert","misassert","overassert","reassert","unassert"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assert#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e61248c83d031ed082","definition":"To maintain or defend, as a cause or a claim, by words or measures; to vindicate a claim or title to.","example":"to assert our rights and liberties","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["remit","deny","deassert"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["assertability","assertable","asserter","assertive","assertment","assert oneself","assertor","counterassert","misassert","overassert","reassert","unasse